DFlash2 drafter model: honor the subclass decoder layer class.

At 6a9c69fa8513 the base DFlashQwen3Model hardcodes DFlashQwen3DecoderLayer
when building self.layers, so the DFlash2 subclass (qwen3_dflash2.py,
registry entry for DFlash2DraftModel) never instantiates its
DFlash2Qwen3DecoderLayer - every published DFlash2 drafter checkpoint then
fails to load with "no module or parameter named 'layers.0.attention_conv'".
Upstream main already routes through self.decoder_layer_cls; this is that
straight backport.

Applies to the vLLM tree:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/dflash2-decoder-layer-cls.patch

--- a/model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash.py
+++ b/model_executor/models/qwen3_dflash.py
@@ -377,6 +377,9 @@
 
 @support_torch_compile
 class DFlashQwen3Model(nn.Module):
+    # port(dflash2): subclasses (DFlash2Qwen3Model) override this so their
+    # conv-augmented decoder layers are what actually gets built.
+    decoder_layer_cls = DFlashQwen3DecoderLayer
     hf_to_vllm_mapper = WeightsMapper(
         orig_to_new_substr={
             "midlayer.": "layers.0.",
@@ -439,7 +442,7 @@
 
         self.layers = nn.ModuleList(
             [
-                DFlashQwen3DecoderLayer(
+                self.decoder_layer_cls(
                     current_vllm_config,
                     config=self.config,
                     layer_idx=layer_idx,
